Abstract = {This paper examines the perceptions of Creek and Turkish Cypriot
   residents of coastal tourism development. Although Butler's hypothesis -
   that there will be an inverse relationship between the level of tourism
   development and perceived impacts for the worse on the social, economic
   and environmental status of the host community - is largely confirmed, a
   significant proportion of uncertain responses in the less developed area
   surveyed lead us to suggest a modification of the Butler hypothesis.
